    "title": "Residual-dimension obstructions for null-projected supersymmetric Yang-Mills theories",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23611588",
    "publication_date": "2026-10-24",
    "description": "<p>We prove necessary residual-dimension conditions for null-projected supersymmetric Yang-Mills constructions under five explicit assumptions N1-N5. A full-corner Majorana-Weyl gaugino gives k at most min(s,t), residual dimension s+t-2k in {2,10}, and signature difference in {8,0,-8}. Direct contractions determine the cubic identity and fermionic source. A separate unitary massless argument gives a helicity-span bound with vanishing tensor charges. The two PDFs contain the same mathematical manuscript in alternative layouts for direct submission to Physical Review D and Annals of Physics; they are not separate papers. General arguments are written in full, with supplementary gamma-matrix checks and disclosed AI assistance. These necessary obstructions do not construct theories in every allowed signature or a nonperturbative quantum model. Sole author: Deep Bhattacharjee. Original preprint: https://hexagonmath.org/2610.00471v1 . Editable sources and verification files: https://github.com/creelie/Paper_4 . No journal submission or acceptance is claimed.</p>",
